      "writtenOn": "2023-05-26T06:56:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "These integers are used both to indicate what the engine *can* (in registerOffloadEngine) and to indicate what the hardware *should* for a given service (in OffloadServiceInfo). The name OFFLOAD_CAPABILITY_* is really only appropriate for the former.\n\nWe could have two separate sets of constants for this (OFFLOAD_CAPABILITY_*, OFFLOAD_TYPE_*). But on the other hand, it seems useful to use the same constant for both capabilities and operations, though. How about we use a more generic name?\n\nSomething like:\n\n    int OFFLOAD_REPLY \u003d 1;\n    int OFFLOAD_FILTER_QUERIES \u003d 1 \u003c\u003c 1;\n    int OFFLOAD_FILTER_REPLIES \u003d 1 \u003c\u003c 2;\n    int OFFLOAD_BYPASS_MULTICAST_FILTERING \u003d 1 \u003c\u003c 3;\n\n    @Retention(RetentionPolicy.SOURCE)\n    @LongDef(flag \u003d false, prefix \u003d {\"OFFLOAD_\"}, value \u003d {\n        OFFLOAD_REPLY,\n        OFFLOAD_FILTER_QUERIES,\n        OFFLOAD_FILTER_REPLIES,\n        OFFLOAD_BYPASS_MULTICAST_FILTERING\n    }\n    @interface OffloadType",
      "range": {
